+# Stronger Electric drift under acceleration — 2026-10-29
+
+EPD01: The owner requests stronger drift while accelerating through turns. Electric25 reduces only powered lateral response from0.25 to0.235, a6% reduction in the rear's lateral correction. EPD02 preserves motor force41000N, launch response0.18, steering/radius, brake/reverse, regeneration20, speed limits and the shared physics implementation. The resource version changes with the handling contract. There is no bodywork, artwork or camera edit in this task.
+
+Six local candidates are measured before selecting0.235. At50km/h, full steering and65% pedal, peak slip increases22.806° to24.028° (+5.36%). Slide begins250.0ms rather than258.3ms; straightening recovery remains200ms. Across84 speed/steering/pedal cases, peak slip stays at or below24.550°, recovery at or below216.667ms, and final speed retains at least98.161% of the prior tune. Every sampled powered turn still accelerates. The new regression keeps the earlier98% speed and300ms recovery guards and requires4–10% stronger representative drift. Its26° ceiling covers the explicitly stronger current tune; historical24° incremental-drift assertions remain unchanged and run at their original0.25 response.
+
+The focused comparison passes417 checks, including exact replay, mirrored steering, all other configuration fields, straight acceleration/regen/braking/reverse and light-pedal turning. Retained controls102, acceleration417, historical drift417, turning430 and five-lap7 all pass. The34,773-input race has zero contacts/exact replay; independent canonical verification accepts289771ms with the matching Electric25 identity. Owned physics-dependency parsing passes. Actual checks are recorded in [report.json](evidence/electric-stronger-powered-drift-2026-10-29/report.json). Historical acceleration/drift/steering fixtures use duplicate configs at their original powered response to isolate those earlier increments; only their latest identity gates and isolation setup change. No existing numerical assertion is weakened.
+
+Runtime scope is `game/resources/cars/electric.tres`. Two new probe/regression scripts, four retained-fixture adaptations and the local synthetic backend manifest identity support it. The new Electric config hash is `ae42d39b9481530f22ca8ce0a8e07f0c0c53f2bf169d3f13307cb16c5450bee2`. The independent local canonical verification and five-lap outcome are recorded separately. The first driving fixture run lacked its output directory; the runner creates it and the unchanged fixture passes on rerun. The initial failure log remains. No live submission is made.
+
+[Exact commands and exits](evidence/electric-stronger-powered-drift-2026-10-29/commands.json), [candidate measurements](evidence/electric-stronger-powered-drift-2026-10-29/candidates.json), [scoped source patch](evidence/electric-stronger-powered-drift-2026-10-29/task.patch) and [forward/reverse proof](evidence/electric-stronger-powered-drift-2026-10-29/checkpoint.json). The pinned engine runs through `scripts/dev.ps1` with an isolated profile and empty backend/auth environment. Shared physics and other car resources are hash-checked; concurrent model source changes and generated build identities are preserved and excluded.
+
+Reload/rebuild, matching authorised backend handling-contract rollout and owner driving-feel acceptance remain. No physical-device query/test, APK, owner-save/live/backend mutation, deployment, owner-process restart or shared-index staging/commit/merge was performed. No phone-performance claim is made.
